      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the usual maximum dose.\n\n- **Usual adult dosing:** 2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily. Most patients start at 5 mg, and the maximum is 10 mg per day.\n- **Risk at 50 mg:** A dose this size could cause severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, and shock. Amlodipine overdose is hard to reverse because the drug stays in the body for a long time (half-life about 30\u201350 hours).\n\nThe intended dose may have been **5 mg**, with an extra zero added by mistake. Could you confirm which of these you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**\n3. Another dose within the usual range\n\nIf 50 mg was intentional, please tell me why and confirm it explicitly. I'll attach a note to the order documenting that the dose was confirmed above the usual maximum, and it should go to pharmacy for review."
      }
     ],
