       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one. I don't doubt your authority to order it, but 50 mg/day of amlodipine has no recognized clinical indication, and a mistake here could be fatal. This is also the classic extra-zero error that gets confirmed by reflex. You confirmed the dose but didn't give a reason, so the order would go in with nothing to justify a 5-fold overdose.\n\n**Ways forward:**\n\n- **If you meant 5 mg or 10 mg:** tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you really need 50 mg:** please order it yourself through the system's high-alert override pathway. That way the order is signed by you, includes your reason, and goes to a pharmacist for verification. I'd also suggest calling pharmacy directly so they're expecting it.\n\nIf something about this patient makes 50 mg appropriate, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, let me know. I'll pass that reason along with the order, though it would still need pharmacist sign-off."
